          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Clear frost mystery and concrete final bee image, but Mara learns the right cause without finding a workable rescue, making the middle feel deliberately stalled.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The failed test, abandoned shelter, and blackened blossoms form a coherent tragic arc; Ivo's promised help is rendered moot by the lack of a method.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000038\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Strong sensory details and a resolved correction about the bees, though the inaccessible notebook and failed trial leave no successful action for Mara to take.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The prose is polished and the loss is vividly shown, but Ivo's availability does not change the outcome because Mara still lacks a usable shelter design.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":9,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":9,\"overall\":9},\"note\":\"Mara tests the complete method, saves two rows within a real time-and-labor limit, and ends on the visible surviving ribbons; this is a fully consequential arc.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000021\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The diagnosis and failed blanket experiment are clear, and the bee-on-weed ending neatly closes the mistaken blame, but all six rows are inevitably lost.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000002\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Mara's distracted partial reading credibly leads to the failed test and loss, with elegant recurring ribbon imagery but limited successful agency.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000037\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A coherent, well-written frost-loss story with a concrete dawn outcome; the fork cannot overcome the missing instructions, so the resolution remains largely passive.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000024\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The causal sequence is understandable and the language is controlled, but the partnered plan never becomes actionable after the trial disproves the blanket setup.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000019\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":9,\"style\":8,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":9,\"overall\":9},\"note\":\"The successful small trial directly enables Mara's difficult choice to finish two shelters, producing a poignant partial success and a vivid final image.\",\"group_id\":1}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":2,\"language\":1,\"overall\":1},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten stories share the same orchard frost threat, correction of blame toward bees, blankets and fork, and ribbon-centered dawn accounting. s000017 and s000019 materially branch into a tested shelter and partial rescue, while s000014, s000028, s000038, s000023, s000021, s000002, s000037, and s000024 end in total loss after the method cannot be used; small differences in notebook access or Ivo's availability do not alter that causal structure.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Mara identifies frost rather than bees as the problem but cannot establish a workable elevated shelter; every marked row freezes, and she releases blame on the bees.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"Mara reads and tests the proper elevated shelter, then can protect only two rows before frost; the two surviving rows visibly mark a partial rescue.\"}]}",
